To: Alex Moreno <alex.moreno@cumuluspay.com>, Jill Park <jill.park@cumuluspay.com>
Cc: Monica Patel <monica@redwood.ai>, Vivek Kulkarni <vivek@redwood.ai>, Grace O'Connor <grace@redwood.ai>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:05:00 -0700
Subject: Re: SDK Turbine onboarding: telemetry, quota & failsafe playbook

Alex — quick answers so your team can review before the call: 

1) Timeouts: the sample uses a conservative default of socket_timeout=8s and request_timeout=25s for generation requests. The reasoning: keep socket < upstream timeouts to allow client-level fast-fail and better CPU reclaim under load. For low-latency routes you can lower request_timeout to 8–12s; for batch or long-context runs we suggest up to 30s.

2) Idempotency: the sdk-turbine snippets include a small helper that generates a UUID idempotency_key when none is provided. Our recommended pattern is integrators supply a stable client token for retriable user actions and let the SDK fallback to generated keys for internal retries. 

3) Soft 429 behavior: treat soft 429 as a signal to slow down and queue with jittered backoff. For user-facing payment steps: surface a transient message and queue the work (don’t immediately show a hard error). For background enrichment pipelines you can pause and resume automatically. We'll include a short sample in the repo that shows a circuit-breaker + queue drain pattern.

See a short inline snippet below (JS-like pseudo) that Vivek prepared for the call: 

// init with telemetry hooks
const client = new RedwoodTurbineClient({
  apiKey: process.env.RDW_KEY,
  sandbox: true,
  telemetry: (evt) => sendTelemetry(evt)
});

async function sendWithRetries(req) {
  const maxAttempts = isIdempotent(req) ? 3 : 2;
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt < maxAttempts) {
    attempt++;
    try {
      return await client.generate(req, {timeoutMs: 25000});
    } catch (err) {
      if (isSoft429(err)) {
        await jitteredBackoff(attempt);
        continue;
      }
      if (attempt >= maxAttempts) throw err;
      await exponentialBackoff(attempt);
    }
  }
}

I'll go through a longer version on the call. If you want, Monica and I can split the runbook review: I'll cover telemetry, retries and client patterns; Monica can cover staging cutover and ops runbook.

— Irene
